1
00:00:00,021 --> 00:00:01,561
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,564 --> 00:00:03,012
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,559 --> 00:00:05,398
(Episode 31)

4
00:00:29,229 --> 00:00:30,501
Hey, Jung A.

5
00:00:31,341 --> 00:00:34,054
It looks like the door is broken.

6
00:00:35,023 --> 00:00:38,238
I need to go to work.
What do I do now? Hurry over.

7
00:00:38,450 --> 00:00:41,752
The kids keep opening and closing it...

8
00:00:41,983 --> 00:00:43,952
and now it seems completely broken.

9
00:00:44,997 --> 00:00:46,242
Okay.

10
00:00:46,985 --> 00:00:48,229
Bye.

11
00:01:23,945 --> 00:01:27,330
I heard Ji Hu skipped breakfast,
so I brought some food.

12
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:30,518
I heard you have meetings all morning.
You can all eat while you work.

13
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:33,670
Thank you. I was planning
to prepare some snacks anyway.

14
00:01:33,730 --> 00:01:35,818
Call me if you ever need anything.

15
00:01:35,952 --> 00:01:37,104
Can I give you my number?

16
00:01:37,334 --> 00:01:39,157
No, that won't be necessary...

17
00:01:41,924 --> 00:01:43,100
Here's my number.

18
00:01:43,427 --> 00:01:44,853
- Okay.
- Don't forget to call me.

19
00:01:44,875 --> 00:01:46,448
- Okay.
- Have a good day.

20
00:01:48,147 --> 00:01:49,583
She didn't have to do all that...

21
00:01:51,469 --> 00:01:53,411
But it looks delicious.

22
00:01:54,429 --> 00:01:56,568
- Good morning.
- Hello.

23
00:01:56,753 --> 00:01:58,884
You must've known I skipped breakfast.

24
00:01:58,943 --> 00:02:00,823
This isn't from me...

25
00:02:00,825 --> 00:02:02,350
I haven't had breakfast either.

26
00:02:02,410 --> 00:02:04,391
I stayed up all night waiting for a call.

27
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,767
Now you know what I'm going through?

28
00:02:10,625 --> 00:02:12,850
- Mr. Go, how did it go?
- Just as expected.

29
00:02:12,934 --> 00:02:14,327
Their schedule is full
through the year after next.

30
00:02:15,025 --> 00:02:17,016
We really need that team to come.

31
00:02:17,110 --> 00:02:18,616
We still have to keep trying.

32
00:02:18,917 --> 00:02:21,029
Exactly. There's no perfect plan.

33
00:02:21,130 --> 00:02:22,754
An opportunity is bound to come up.

34
00:02:23,326 --> 00:02:25,608
If we remain on standby,
we'll get our chance.

35
00:02:26,290 --> 00:02:28,760
Mi Joo, where are these sandwiches from?

36
00:02:28,990 --> 00:02:30,552
They're better than what we usually have.

37
00:02:30,555 --> 00:02:32,889
- I didn't buy these.
- You didn't?

38
00:02:32,892 --> 00:02:35,605
They were already here when I arrived.

39
00:02:35,607 --> 00:02:36,914
Your girlfriend brought them.

40
00:02:36,917 --> 00:02:39,521
- Do Hee.
- I knew it...

41
00:02:39,612 --> 00:02:42,463
Your fiancée is looking after you.
I'm really jealous.

42
00:02:43,572 --> 00:02:45,771
We've booked the Strasbourg String Trio.

43
00:02:46,842 --> 00:02:47,842
Okay.

44
00:02:49,048 --> 00:02:52,050
Our hard work for over a month
has finally paid off.

45
00:02:57,075 --> 00:03:00,185
Play the yellow one. Good job.

46
00:03:00,187 --> 00:03:03,562
Now play the red one. That's right.

47
00:03:03,856 --> 00:03:05,275
Where's the green one?

48
00:03:05,710 --> 00:03:07,939
The music teacher is here.

49
00:03:08,496 --> 00:03:10,387
Thank you, Second Mother.

50
00:03:11,014 --> 00:03:12,252
Thank you.

51
00:03:13,285 --> 00:03:16,580
You little rascal. You're so adorable.

52
00:03:17,350 --> 00:03:19,789
Did they say not to give herbal medicine?

53
00:03:21,153 --> 00:03:23,890
Plain porridge alone won't be enough.

54
00:03:24,492 --> 00:03:26,093
Want me to recommend a good doctor?

55
00:03:26,741 --> 00:03:28,206
The doctor advised against it.

56
00:03:28,512 --> 00:03:31,199
Mother happens to know a good doctor.

57
00:03:36,551 --> 00:03:41,654
O Reum, it looks like your grandma
is in a good mood.

58
00:03:45,317 --> 00:03:48,037
- The yellow one.
- Mother, you look prettier these days.

59
00:03:48,517 --> 00:03:50,293
It's because of O Reum, isn't it?

60
00:03:50,295 --> 00:03:52,837
That's right. It's all thanks to O Reum.

61
00:03:54,070 --> 00:03:57,482
You make me so happy
that I don't even need to eat.

62
00:03:58,450 --> 00:04:00,484
I'm also glad you stopped clubbing.

63
00:04:01,254 --> 00:04:02,500
My club...

64
00:04:02,925 --> 00:04:04,985
I really miss it.

65
00:04:06,202 --> 00:04:08,425
Do you? Shall I go with you?

66
00:04:09,254 --> 00:04:12,378
- Shall we take O Reum with us?
- That sounds fun.

67
00:04:12,432 --> 00:04:14,833
Shall we go as soon as possible?

68
00:04:19,392 --> 00:04:20,739
Thanks for the sandwiches this morning.

69
00:04:21,192 --> 00:04:22,906
You don't need to do so much for me.

70
00:04:23,048 --> 00:04:24,294
Don't feel like you owe me.

71
00:04:24,386 --> 00:04:25,759
You weren't the only one up all night.

72
00:04:26,410 --> 00:04:28,311
I was up all night painting too,

73
00:04:28,512 --> 00:04:31,896
and since I needed breakfast anyway,
I thought I'd bring you some too.

74
00:04:32,547 --> 00:04:33,912
You really were up all night.

75
00:04:34,355 --> 00:04:35,954
What are you painting? I want to see it.

76
00:04:35,957 --> 00:04:38,543
I'll show you once it's done.

77
00:04:38,614 --> 00:04:40,092
You know I like your artwork, right?

78
00:04:40,909 --> 00:04:42,332
You used to.

79
00:04:43,150 --> 00:04:45,212
But now you like Na Ji Ni's art, right?

80
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:48,791
It's because she's doing well
at your father's company too.

81
00:04:48,846 --> 00:04:50,823
You and Ji Ni are different.

82
00:04:50,938 --> 00:04:52,406
I don't like Na Ji Ni's art.

83
00:04:53,052 --> 00:04:54,804
The effortlessly gifted type?

84
00:04:55,141 --> 00:04:57,148
- I can't stand her.
- Do Hee.

85
00:04:57,351 --> 00:05:00,214
I'm tired of trying so hard.
Stop nagging me.

86
00:05:00,568 --> 00:05:01,845
You weren't this way in London.

87
00:05:01,847 --> 00:05:03,462
It's because you worked hard back then.

88
00:05:04,083 --> 00:05:06,014
I won't try anymore. I don't want to.

89
00:05:06,672 --> 00:05:08,300
Do you know how it feels to be a B?

90
00:05:08,513 --> 00:05:10,460
Neither an A nor a C.

91
00:05:10,972 --> 00:05:14,320
Giving up feels like a waste,
but I lack the talent to keep going.

92
00:05:15,587 --> 00:05:17,557
This is driving me crazy.

93
00:05:18,585 --> 00:05:20,245
Ji Ni puts in a lot of effort too.

94
00:05:20,247 --> 00:05:22,896
She says ideas come to her
as soon as she picks up a brush.

95
00:05:22,916 --> 00:05:23,964
That crazy girl.

96
00:05:25,752 --> 00:05:28,812
Sometimes, a blank page makes me feel
like I'm in a mental hospital.

97
00:05:31,812 --> 00:05:33,579
You must've been really stressed, Do Hee.

98
00:05:33,922 --> 00:05:34,937
Let's stop talking about it.

99
00:05:35,987 --> 00:05:38,943
I came back to Korea to avoid mom,
but you're acting just like her.

100
00:05:38,985 --> 00:05:40,479
Always nagging me.

101
00:05:41,882 --> 00:05:43,069
I'm sorry.

102
00:05:43,332 --> 00:05:44,592
Don't think about your mother.

103
00:05:44,698 --> 00:05:46,849
I depend on mom's money
and dad's name for my career,

104
00:05:46,851 --> 00:05:48,385
so how can I not worry?

105
00:05:49,152 --> 00:05:52,229
That's why you should marry me soon.

106
00:05:52,298 --> 00:05:53,787
There you go again.

107
00:05:55,229 --> 00:05:57,730
- What?
- You're a good person,

108
00:05:58,058 --> 00:06:01,010
but your mother will only accept me
because of my father.

109
00:06:15,193 --> 00:06:16,229
What are you doing?

110
00:06:17,287 --> 00:06:20,810
I'm clearing out your expired cosmetics.

111
00:06:21,065 --> 00:06:23,292
Don't touch them. I still use them all.

112
00:06:23,587 --> 00:06:24,666
You can use mine.

113
00:06:25,204 --> 00:06:28,329
Your legal husband bought them,
so feel free to use them.

114
00:06:31,272 --> 00:06:33,304
- Na Se Ri.
- What?

115
00:06:33,962 --> 00:06:35,722
Why are you getting so worked up?

116
00:06:38,581 --> 00:06:41,928
This is pretty. What is it?

117
00:06:41,930 --> 00:06:43,305
I told you to stop.

118
00:06:43,612 --> 00:06:46,235
- A man must've bought it for you.
- That's not true.

119
00:06:46,964 --> 00:06:50,421
I'm the only one in this family
who pays any attention to you.

120
00:06:50,652 --> 00:06:52,992
I could tell right away
that you're dating someone.

121
00:06:53,170 --> 00:06:54,884
Your sons haven't noticed, right?

122
00:06:54,989 --> 00:06:58,252
Mai is so wrapped up in O Reum
that she doesn't pay attention to you.

123
00:06:59,330 --> 00:07:01,503
Have you lost your mind?

124
00:07:01,690 --> 00:07:03,583
What on earth are you talking about?

125
00:07:03,792 --> 00:07:05,418
You think I don't know you?

126
00:07:06,121 --> 00:07:09,981
It's written all over your face.
You have the ease of a woman in love.

127
00:07:10,750 --> 00:07:13,637
You're smiling despite everything
that's going on.

128
00:07:14,761 --> 00:07:16,475
You're not that type of person.

129
00:07:16,669 --> 00:07:19,414
Even at the hospital, you said
we should go home together...

130
00:07:19,514 --> 00:07:20,577
I found that strange.

131
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:22,029
I only did that because of O Reum...

132
00:07:22,063 --> 00:07:25,667
You always used to say things
that hurt me deeply.

133
00:07:26,232 --> 00:07:30,312
On my way here, I was more worried
about dealing with you than Seung Woo.

134
00:07:30,429 --> 00:07:32,475
Fine. Then get out.

135
00:07:32,950 --> 00:07:36,708
Since you know me so well,
I might as well show my true colors.

136
00:07:36,888 --> 00:07:39,875
I've been wondering how to tell you
to get out anyway.

137
00:07:41,536 --> 00:07:46,008
I'll give you free relationship advice,
so don't keep it all to yourself.

138
00:07:47,350 --> 00:07:50,783
I should go look for a student to teach.

139
00:07:59,712 --> 00:08:01,146
She thinks I've changed?

140
00:08:03,823 --> 00:08:05,183
What nonsense.

141
00:08:05,652 --> 00:08:07,291
As if I don't know what she's plotting.

142
00:08:07,881 --> 00:08:08,968
That sly fox.

143
00:08:10,665 --> 00:08:12,479
I'm only holding back for O Reum's sake.

144
00:08:37,343 --> 00:08:39,914
I met the student you referred to me.
It went well.

145
00:08:40,164 --> 00:08:43,523
I'll get a bonus if I prepare them well
for the arts high school entrance exam.

146
00:08:43,642 --> 00:08:45,820
- Isn't that great?
- That's good news.

147
00:08:46,030 --> 00:08:47,707
The student is lucky too.

148
00:08:47,710 --> 00:08:50,766
They'll be learning from someone
as talented and famous as you.

149
00:08:50,896 --> 00:08:52,154
This is a secret, but...

150
00:08:52,264 --> 00:08:54,521
I know the teacher in charge.

151
00:08:55,498 --> 00:08:57,089
I told their mother about it too.

152
00:08:57,629 --> 00:08:59,056
How are things at home?

153
00:08:59,856 --> 00:09:02,471
It's my fault, so I have to live with it,

154
00:09:02,652 --> 00:09:04,791
but I came up with a clever plan
for Ji Ni's sake.

155
00:09:05,187 --> 00:09:08,081
- Really?
- I guess that's what mothers do.

156
00:09:08,110 --> 00:09:09,410
There's nothing I wouldn't do.

157
00:09:10,130 --> 00:09:12,575
You should get married soon
and have a child of your own.

158
00:09:12,606 --> 00:09:15,351
Having kids forces you
to become a better person.

159
00:09:16,715 --> 00:09:18,960
Yes, they do.

160
00:09:19,632 --> 00:09:22,271
My brother was an amazing man too,

161
00:09:22,324 --> 00:09:24,610
but he became even better
after his son was born.

162
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:29,869
I think having a kid is what makes me
the kindest person in the world.

163
00:09:31,870 --> 00:09:35,823
It's moving just to see
how much you've changed.

164
00:09:36,612 --> 00:09:38,312
Your husband used
to do everything for you.

165
00:09:38,383 --> 00:09:39,751
Yeah, he did.

166
00:09:40,378 --> 00:09:41,595
Now I do it myself.

167
00:09:42,450 --> 00:09:43,705
You can do it.

168
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:56,014
Are you alone?

169
00:09:56,951 --> 00:09:57,951
Where's my father-in-law?

170
00:09:58,513 --> 00:10:01,549
- He has a lot of outside meetings today.
- What about Ji Hu?

171
00:10:04,223 --> 00:10:07,371
You were always sticking your nose in,
so I thought you knew everything.

172
00:10:08,981 --> 00:10:09,981
What's going on?

173
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:13,960
What's wrong?

174
00:10:15,233 --> 00:10:16,979
Don't get so worked up.

175
00:10:17,510 --> 00:10:19,093
I'm not like that with you anymore.

176
00:10:19,095 --> 00:10:20,732
I won't take it anymore, either.

177
00:10:20,774 --> 00:10:23,583
Of course not. You're Na Ji Ni, after all.

178
00:10:25,528 --> 00:10:27,949
That's why I'm here to ask you a favor.

179
00:10:31,170 --> 00:10:33,618
Could you leave this place?

180
00:10:34,686 --> 00:10:35,869
I'll pay you a salary.

181
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:38,471
I'll pay you as if you still worked here,
even if you get another job.

182
00:10:38,757 --> 00:10:42,008
You'll get hired anywhere.
You're a genius.

183
00:10:42,922 --> 00:10:44,080
I'm not falling for that.

184
00:10:44,446 --> 00:10:47,854
I remember how you pushed me around,
calling me a genius and gaslighting me.

185
00:10:48,721 --> 00:10:50,611
I even got fired from the center
because of you.

186
00:10:51,448 --> 00:10:52,721
You really...

187
00:10:53,170 --> 00:10:54,770
Let's get our facts straight.

188
00:10:55,030 --> 00:10:56,778
It was your mom's fault, not mine.

189
00:10:56,832 --> 00:10:58,604
Because your mom was a mistress.

190
00:10:59,835 --> 00:11:01,650
What?

191
00:11:04,616 --> 00:11:05,806
Ma'am?

192
00:11:05,936 --> 00:11:08,258
You came all the way here
to harass my daughter?

193
00:11:08,770 --> 00:11:12,218
- Haven't you done enough?
- Mom, don't.

194
00:11:12,277 --> 00:11:13,625
Seriously!

195
00:11:13,983 --> 00:11:16,530
I'd be crying from misery
if I didn't have my mom.

196
00:11:18,256 --> 00:11:19,709
I have my dad too.

197
00:11:19,755 --> 00:11:21,086
If you have nothing to say, leave.

198
00:11:21,130 --> 00:11:22,581
There's nothing for us to talk about.

199
00:11:22,630 --> 00:11:24,458
I have plenty to say to you.

200
00:11:25,452 --> 00:11:28,173
- And plenty I can do.
- Bring it.

201
00:11:28,585 --> 00:11:30,548
You think I'll lose to someone like you?

202
00:11:30,730 --> 00:11:32,208
I've got nothing left to lose.

203
00:11:32,269 --> 00:11:33,269
Ma'am,

204
00:11:34,753 --> 00:11:36,564
stop messing with me.

205
00:11:37,692 --> 00:11:39,631
I hear your husband died
and your business went under,

206
00:11:40,042 --> 00:11:42,548
and now you're really down on your luck.

207
00:11:43,351 --> 00:11:46,589
Why do you think that is? Think about it.

208
00:11:47,065 --> 00:11:48,760
Still don't realize you're being punished?

209
00:11:48,762 --> 00:11:50,530
I did nothing wrong to you. Get lost.

210
00:11:54,072 --> 00:11:56,200
I was going to ask you for a favor,

211
00:11:57,083 --> 00:11:58,485
but not today.

212
00:12:05,347 --> 00:12:07,139
Are you still letting her push you around?

213
00:12:07,191 --> 00:12:08,737
Why didn't you tell me?

214
00:12:09,504 --> 00:12:10,715
This is the first time.

215
00:12:11,410 --> 00:12:14,336
It's your first time here too.
Why did you come?

216
00:12:15,670 --> 00:12:17,725
I came to take you home after work.

217
00:12:18,010 --> 00:12:19,825
- I'm not going.
- If you don't,

218
00:12:20,147 --> 00:12:22,846
I'll sleep at the studio with you.
I can't leave you alone.

219
00:12:23,590 --> 00:12:26,635
Go home, spend time with O Reum,
and rest somewhere that feels like home.

220
00:12:26,710 --> 00:12:27,907
That's how you'll be able to work.

221
00:12:29,094 --> 00:12:31,103
- That's not our home.
- It's our home.

222
00:12:31,141 --> 00:12:32,770
Mom, this is why Do Hee...

223
00:12:36,072 --> 00:12:37,072
I...

224
00:12:37,435 --> 00:12:38,980
have more lessons now too.

225
00:12:39,692 --> 00:12:42,439
Just wait a little.
I'll get us a proper place.

226
00:12:44,981 --> 00:12:45,981
Okay?

227
00:12:56,690 --> 00:12:58,666
- Ji Ni.
- What?

228
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:01,663
- Were you waiting for me?
- Yeah.

229
00:13:01,776 --> 00:13:04,404
- Draw for me.
- Okay.

230
00:13:04,452 --> 00:13:06,687
I'm going to dry my hair first.

231
00:13:07,107 --> 00:13:10,458
- Come back soon.
- Okay.

232
00:13:13,511 --> 00:13:15,393
I'm glad you came too.

233
00:13:16,164 --> 00:13:17,468
I'll make you something good.

234
00:13:17,470 --> 00:13:20,052
It's Vietnamese. Do you like cilantro?

235
00:13:20,378 --> 00:13:22,012
Yes, I do.

236
00:13:22,576 --> 00:13:25,698
- O Reum, go play with Ji Ni.
- Okay.

237
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:38,840
How about this?

238
00:13:39,696 --> 00:13:42,265
- But what about you?
- The master bedroom.

239
00:13:42,463 --> 00:13:43,937
Are you staying with Yeong Ju?

240
00:13:44,151 --> 00:13:46,277
- She's okay with it?
- Of course.

241
00:13:46,585 --> 00:13:48,718
Thanks to you, it's all over for us.

242
00:13:49,157 --> 00:13:50,993
Besides, your dad's gone now.

243
00:13:52,513 --> 00:13:54,843
She moved on from your dad
a long time ago.

244
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:58,989
- My gut says she's dating someone.
- What?

245
00:14:00,547 --> 00:14:01,890
You're jumping to conclusions
again, right?

246
00:14:02,138 --> 00:14:03,435
If not, then never mind.

247
00:14:03,886 --> 00:14:07,267
Either way,
the fact is we have nowhere to go.

248
00:14:07,861 --> 00:14:10,562
We can't afford to worry
about anyone else's situation.

249
00:14:12,138 --> 00:14:13,138
Yes.

250
00:14:16,485 --> 00:14:18,057
You're here.

251
00:14:22,018 --> 00:14:24,702
These are the places I picked out today.

252
00:14:25,475 --> 00:14:27,696
- Pick one and move out.
- You little...

253
00:14:28,572 --> 00:14:30,447
This isn't right.

254
00:14:30,472 --> 00:14:32,501
How can we all live together?

255
00:14:32,692 --> 00:14:33,890
If people see us,

256
00:14:35,268 --> 00:14:36,935
they'll think we're filming some comedy.

257
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:38,243
Who cares what they think?

258
00:14:38,268 --> 00:14:40,043
I have nowhere else to go right now.

259
00:14:40,068 --> 00:14:41,068
That's why I'm telling you...

260
00:14:43,598 --> 00:14:44,776
to pick one and move out.

261
00:14:44,901 --> 00:14:46,151
No. You move out.

262
00:14:52,645 --> 00:14:54,652
This place is too far from Ji Ni's work.

263
00:14:54,676 --> 00:14:56,113
How many bedrooms does this one have?

264
00:14:56,138 --> 00:14:57,588
It needs to have at least three.

265
00:14:57,714 --> 00:14:59,163
I need a walk-in closet too.

266
00:15:01,213 --> 00:15:03,497
Anyway, I don't like it. It's not safe.

267
00:15:03,623 --> 00:15:05,313
What's so scary about a studio apartment?

268
00:15:05,879 --> 00:15:08,203
All my married friends
live in places like that.

269
00:15:08,772 --> 00:15:09,988
Please!

270
00:15:10,512 --> 00:15:12,068
Let's be reasonable.

271
00:15:12,233 --> 00:15:14,575
They're newlyweds with husbands.

272
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:17,584
Do you know how scary it is
without a husband around?

273
00:15:17,712 --> 00:15:19,758
The shop owners come in,

274
00:15:19,782 --> 00:15:21,957
and just anyone can walk right in.

275
00:15:22,549 --> 00:15:23,898
Seriously!

276
00:15:26,114 --> 00:15:29,176
If you ask me, you're scarier, CEO.

277
00:15:29,201 --> 00:15:30,632
Why are you calling me CEO?

278
00:15:30,992 --> 00:15:33,882
Anyway, I'm not leaving
until we find an apartment.

279
00:15:35,112 --> 00:15:37,503
How are you going to get an apartment?

280
00:15:42,038 --> 00:15:43,038
What?

281
00:15:43,238 --> 00:15:45,387
- Sell this and buy me an apartment.
- What?

282
00:15:45,412 --> 00:15:47,318
I hear people get paid a lot...

283
00:15:47,610 --> 00:15:49,681
for donating bone marrow.

284
00:15:49,706 --> 00:15:51,186
That's illegal.

285
00:15:51,219 --> 00:15:53,320
Then wait until I can afford one myself.

286
00:15:57,292 --> 00:15:58,799
Why are there so many stairs?

287
00:16:02,038 --> 00:16:04,114
This is really getting on my nerves.

288
00:16:09,685 --> 00:16:11,826
Whenever he came by,

289
00:16:11,850 --> 00:16:13,859
he'd say he couldn't stand living
because of Seung Woo.

290
00:16:13,884 --> 00:16:15,072
He meant it.

291
00:16:17,457 --> 00:16:18,724
I'm lonely.

292
00:16:19,585 --> 00:16:23,684
They say couples who are close
remarry soon after losing a spouse.

293
00:16:24,314 --> 00:16:25,893
Seriously!

294
00:16:26,389 --> 00:16:27,393
Fine!

295
00:16:27,424 --> 00:16:29,952
We weren't close, so I never remarried.
Happy now?

296
00:16:29,977 --> 00:16:32,693
Yeong Ju, that's not what I meant.

297
00:16:33,109 --> 00:16:34,184
Did that hit a nerve?

298
00:16:35,952 --> 00:16:36,952
You don't know, right?

299
00:16:37,845 --> 00:16:39,913
When you were away performing overseas,

300
00:16:39,938 --> 00:16:42,407
he'd sometimes come by, eat, and leave.

301
00:16:42,432 --> 00:16:44,313
He even complained that you couldn't cook.

302
00:16:44,910 --> 00:16:47,287
- You're lying.
- Believe whatever you want.

303
00:16:47,290 --> 00:16:49,170
I'm just telling you the truth.

304
00:16:49,558 --> 00:16:50,878
When he got a call from you,

305
00:16:51,334 --> 00:16:53,880
he answered it out on the porch.

306
00:16:54,372 --> 00:16:57,034
It was during your tour in Europe.

307
00:16:57,298 --> 00:16:59,494
Ji Ni was probably staying
with your family then too.

308
00:16:59,756 --> 00:17:00,756
He told you...

309
00:17:01,250 --> 00:17:03,090
he was at work, but he was lying.

310
00:17:03,115 --> 00:17:04,336
Why are you telling me this now?

311
00:17:04,377 --> 00:17:06,678
Because you'd have grabbed me
by the collar if I'd told you then.

312
00:17:09,701 --> 00:17:11,726
That two-faced bastard!

313
00:17:14,940 --> 00:17:17,167
So he did that while I was away.

314
00:17:23,942 --> 00:17:25,752
It's hot. Seriously!

315
00:17:37,538 --> 00:17:39,419
Let's make Korean soy-braised beef too.

316
00:17:39,444 --> 00:17:41,327
- I'll pack some in Ji Ni's lunch.
- Right.

317
00:17:41,352 --> 00:17:42,683
O Reum likes it too.

318
00:17:42,881 --> 00:17:44,325
Really? Then...

319
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:47,079
Yeah, let's buy some.

320
00:17:48,458 --> 00:17:50,933
Second Mother, let's get some sashimi too.

321
00:17:51,732 --> 00:17:53,687
My husband's been too skinny lately.

322
00:17:53,861 --> 00:17:56,565
Sashimi sounds good.
Then we should have some soju too.

323
00:17:57,278 --> 00:17:58,594
Second Mother,

324
00:17:58,980 --> 00:18:00,258
can you hold your liquor?

325
00:18:02,479 --> 00:18:05,685
Could you please stop calling me
"Second Mother?"

326
00:18:05,709 --> 00:18:08,559
- People are watching.
- Why? It's true.

327
00:18:08,575 --> 00:18:10,979
My mother-in-law, my second mother-in-law.

328
00:18:14,785 --> 00:18:16,081
You're trying to get a rise out of me,
aren't you?

329
00:18:16,488 --> 00:18:18,288
What? No.

330
00:18:18,312 --> 00:18:21,973
I'm just helping you settle your account.

331
00:18:23,719 --> 00:18:25,669
What are you helping with?

332
00:18:27,225 --> 00:18:30,846
When I was little,
my mom in Ho Chi Minh used to say,

333
00:18:30,952 --> 00:18:33,981
"People need clear rewards
and punishments."

334
00:18:34,212 --> 00:18:37,275
If I'd done five things wrong
and seven things right,

335
00:18:37,299 --> 00:18:40,140
my mom would give me two pieces of candy.

336
00:18:40,252 --> 00:18:43,664
So if you get humiliated,

337
00:18:43,688 --> 00:18:45,787
your punishment gets reduced. Why?

338
00:18:46,002 --> 00:18:47,640
Because you were punished.

339
00:18:47,851 --> 00:18:49,896
Your Ho Chi Minh mom is pretty wise.

340
00:18:51,807 --> 00:18:52,867
You like that, Yeong Ju?

341
00:18:53,605 --> 00:18:55,194
I do. Serves you right.

342
00:18:58,431 --> 00:19:02,177
"Rewards and punishments." You really
put a lot of thought into your nonsense.

343
00:19:02,295 --> 00:19:04,763
- You're lucky to have so many moms.
- Right.

344
00:19:04,788 --> 00:19:06,602
I've got plenty of moms.

345
00:19:07,698 --> 00:19:08,954
Mother, the watermelon!

346
00:19:12,873 --> 00:19:15,173
This is what I used to eat
when I studied abroad.

347
00:19:42,517 --> 00:19:44,142
Why do you keep coming over?

348
00:19:44,561 --> 00:19:45,967
That room isn't big enough for two.

349
00:19:46,243 --> 00:19:48,619
Ji Ni's working all night.

350
00:19:49,456 --> 00:19:50,643
Seriously.

351
00:19:51,656 --> 00:19:54,049
Yeong Ju, are those your pajamas?

352
00:19:55,056 --> 00:19:56,287
What's wrong with it?

353
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:01,948
I didn't dress like this
when I had a husband.

354
00:20:01,965 --> 00:20:03,389
You turned me into a nun.

355
00:20:03,391 --> 00:20:05,181
Who said anything? I didn't say a word.

356
00:20:05,190 --> 00:20:06,456
You said it with your eyes!

357
00:20:06,895 --> 00:20:08,031
Good. At least you know.

358
00:20:15,073 --> 00:20:16,523
That's so petty. Seriously!

359
00:20:22,045 --> 00:20:23,505
Does your hand hurt?

360
00:20:23,527 --> 00:20:25,495
Do you have eyes in the back of your head?

361
00:20:25,885 --> 00:20:27,635
Of course it hurts. That's why I came.

362
00:20:27,652 --> 00:20:30,323
If I'd had anyone else to turn to,
would I have come here?

363
00:20:44,879 --> 00:20:47,318
Yeong Ju, do you still get your period?

364
00:20:47,326 --> 00:20:49,221
Have you already gone through menopause?

365
00:20:49,904 --> 00:20:51,100
Of course.

366
00:20:52,483 --> 00:20:54,668
You're still young.

367
00:20:54,876 --> 00:20:56,304
Seriously, date someone.

368
00:20:56,958 --> 00:21:00,323
I'm still so young,
yet I've lived my whole life like a nun.

369
00:21:00,338 --> 00:21:01,510
Thanks to someone.

370
00:21:15,564 --> 00:21:18,881
When you raise the pitch,
focus more on your vocal projection.

371
00:21:18,906 --> 00:21:21,130
Rather than barely reaching the note,

372
00:21:21,154 --> 00:21:25,772
singing with a fuller sound
will help you hit the pitch accurately.

373
00:21:25,798 --> 00:21:28,270
Focus on your head voice
and mouth shape too.

374
00:21:28,294 --> 00:21:29,523
Shall we begin?

375
00:22:05,325 --> 00:22:09,171
I think I've been unlucky as a woman.

376
00:22:09,838 --> 00:22:12,256
I used to feel it was unfair,

377
00:22:12,784 --> 00:22:15,560
but at some point, I started to feel free.

378
00:22:16,634 --> 00:22:17,783
Is that strange?

379
00:22:18,072 --> 00:22:21,158
But wouldn't it be a shame...

380
00:22:21,527 --> 00:22:22,902
to erase the woman in you?

381
00:22:24,385 --> 00:22:25,810
The word "woman..."

382
00:22:26,316 --> 00:22:27,844
feels so unfamiliar.

383
00:22:31,005 --> 00:22:32,465
Do you really have no regrets?

384
00:22:32,872 --> 00:22:35,323
It would be a lie to say I have none.

385
00:22:36,118 --> 00:22:37,279
When spring comes...

386
00:22:37,618 --> 00:22:39,687
and I see the flowers in full bloom,

387
00:22:40,251 --> 00:22:42,637
I'd think,
"Lucky you. You bloom every year."

388
00:22:42,972 --> 00:22:44,681
"While I'm coming to an end like this."

389
00:22:45,372 --> 00:22:47,862
There were times I felt that way.

390
00:22:52,197 --> 00:22:53,854
After my husband left...

391
00:22:54,057 --> 00:22:55,879
and my younger son was injured,

392
00:22:56,462 --> 00:22:59,933
watching the boy who dreamed of becoming
a soccer player lose his dream,

393
00:23:00,535 --> 00:23:02,225
I opened a singing class.

394
00:23:03,411 --> 00:23:04,604
Otherwise,

395
00:23:05,491 --> 00:23:07,512
I thought I'd lose my mind.

396
00:23:12,012 --> 00:23:14,994
It feels like it happened so long ago.

397
00:23:17,512 --> 00:23:19,546
It's heartbreaking just to hear it.

398
00:23:21,336 --> 00:23:22,919
You're truly amazing.

399
00:23:23,878 --> 00:23:25,496
Did you know that I admired you...

400
00:23:26,344 --> 00:23:27,948
and then fell in love with you?

401
00:23:29,607 --> 00:23:30,777
With me?

402
00:23:31,519 --> 00:23:33,469
What is there to admire about me?

403
00:23:33,905 --> 00:23:35,737
At first, I fell for your singing,

404
00:23:35,988 --> 00:23:39,106
and later, I fell for the way
you face life.

405
00:23:39,801 --> 00:23:41,251
You're too kind.

406
00:23:42,145 --> 00:23:44,928
Enough about me. As for you, Sa Bin,

407
00:23:44,952 --> 00:23:48,275
before it's too late,
you should start a family as a man...

408
00:23:48,299 --> 00:23:49,916
and become a father.

409
00:23:52,577 --> 00:23:54,379
Am I not a man?

410
00:23:55,274 --> 00:23:56,839
Am I a woman?

411
00:23:57,732 --> 00:23:58,832
Sa Bin,

412
00:23:59,475 --> 00:24:00,837
don't forget.

413
00:24:01,155 --> 00:24:02,733
I'm a grandmother.

414
00:24:02,973 --> 00:24:04,896
That's just a family relationship.

415
00:24:05,036 --> 00:24:06,344
I'm talking about us...

416
00:24:06,609 --> 00:24:08,398
as a man and a woman.

417
00:24:21,625 --> 00:24:24,041
The day you burst into tears
the moment you saw me,

418
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:25,393
do you remember?

419
00:24:26,712 --> 00:24:29,207
How could I forget that day?

420
00:24:29,258 --> 00:24:30,477
From that day on,

421
00:24:31,466 --> 00:24:32,781
in my heart,

422
00:24:33,953 --> 00:24:35,280
it was Day One.

423
00:24:39,312 --> 00:24:41,166
That day...

424
00:24:41,191 --> 00:24:43,810
Would you have cried
if it had been someone else?

425
00:24:45,562 --> 00:24:47,258
Not exactly, but...

426
00:24:49,498 --> 00:24:50,580
that day...

427
00:24:51,449 --> 00:24:53,553
was just so hard for me.

428
00:24:55,599 --> 00:24:56,766
Actually...

429
00:24:58,240 --> 00:25:01,017
My husband had another woman.

430
00:25:01,572 --> 00:25:03,227
And they had a daughter.

431
00:25:04,178 --> 00:25:08,280
That girl was the one
who donated her bone marrow to O Reum.

432
00:25:08,705 --> 00:25:10,786
So that's why
you feel unlucky as a woman...

433
00:25:11,112 --> 00:25:14,004
and feel that your life
as a woman is over?

434
00:25:19,698 --> 00:25:21,114
And on a day like that...

435
00:25:21,762 --> 00:25:23,000
you happened to meet me.

436
00:25:24,972 --> 00:25:26,851
Even if we'd arranged to meet,

437
00:25:27,018 --> 00:25:28,661
we couldn't have met like that.

438
00:25:30,885 --> 00:25:32,592
Isn't that even more like fate?

439
00:25:41,718 --> 00:25:44,157
Here come the noodles!

440
00:25:45,578 --> 00:25:48,190
Let's see who can get more to stick.

441
00:25:56,485 --> 00:25:57,874
I'll put it right here!

442
00:25:57,899 --> 00:26:00,564
You little rascal. Why are you so cute?

443
00:26:00,983 --> 00:26:02,803
You're just like your grandpa.

444
00:26:03,033 --> 00:26:06,034
Just like your grandpa.

445
00:26:09,580 --> 00:26:11,386
O Reum, here come the noodles!

446
00:26:14,059 --> 00:26:15,592
Let's go together.

447
00:26:15,702 --> 00:26:17,943
- What's wrong?
- I don't know.

448
00:26:18,042 --> 00:26:19,153
I'm confused.

449
00:26:19,450 --> 00:26:20,743
Let's not see each other again.

450
00:26:21,028 --> 00:26:22,028
Yeong Ju!

451
00:26:22,766 --> 00:26:23,766
I...

452
00:26:24,050 --> 00:26:26,235
I don't want to lose my peace.

453
00:26:26,238 --> 00:26:29,349
You're too young to settle
for being a grandmother.

454
00:26:45,432 --> 00:26:48,332
You should go back now.
The kids will see you.

455
00:26:48,651 --> 00:26:50,818
Okay. You go in first.

456
00:27:06,342 --> 00:27:08,993
Here, let me try.

457
00:27:09,018 --> 00:27:11,418
- Tell me the number.
- No, it's okay.

458
00:27:13,290 --> 00:27:15,887
- Why can't you open the door?
- What?

459
00:27:20,342 --> 00:27:22,301
Sa Bin.

460
00:27:54,132 --> 00:27:57,487
(Family Register)

461
00:27:57,511 --> 00:27:58,608
We need to talk.

462
00:27:58,632 --> 00:28:00,148
So you're the musician
Sa Bin was talking about.

463
00:28:00,173 --> 00:28:02,247
Please help me.
I've never felt this way before.

464
00:28:02,272 --> 00:28:04,728
Na Ji Ni, let's see this through
to the end.

465
00:28:04,752 --> 00:28:06,887
I know who it is.
I have a pretty good idea too.

466
00:28:06,912 --> 00:28:08,292
I'm going to tell him
to cut ties with you.

467
00:28:08,317 --> 00:28:10,405
That's my condition
for accepting his love.

468
00:28:10,430 --> 00:28:11,592
Don't be ridiculous.

469
00:28:11,617 --> 00:28:13,069
Mom said she wasn't interested in men.

470
00:28:13,094 --> 00:28:15,372
You can't destroy our relationship.

471
00:28:15,397 --> 00:28:18,036
Let's see whether I can or not.

472
00:28:20,058 --> 00:28:22,058
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
